R-CV1 R-CV2 R-CV3 R-CV5 R-CV6 R-AP80 R-AP5 R-AP19 R-AP47 R-AP50 R-NS1 R-IX4: Nightlies.list_registry! with the fake Fx (tests/commands/L2Registry.roc, entry registry, the word nightlies). Origin 9 gives 6 rows: log 1 a bad sha256, 2 the month-name tag (July), 3 a macOS row, 4 the newest linux row, 5 an asset name that is not a safe path part, 6 a tag that is not a nightly.
Run 1 (linux_x86_64): the request calls of RegistryToolchains.list! (after=0, one page, one write), then one db_query of the pinned rows and one db_write with the 2 new rows that have an asset and a sha256 (log 2 and 4), with the source registry (R-CV5) in compat.tsv. The 4 releases are in the order of R-NS1 (the July tag first), published_at in seconds, size 0, the GitHub URL of the tag and the asset, sha256 none for the bad one, no asset for the unsafe name.
Run 2: after=6 (the largest kept log index), an empty page, no write of the rows, db_query pinned=2 and no db_write (R-CV6: a recorded row stays). Run 3 (macos_x86_64): the same request, 1 release and 1 new pin. Run 4 (log=2): the rows above 2 are hidden, so 2 releases and the query of 1 pinned row (a hidden row is not seen: Q4 of slice 204).
Run 5 (offline): no request, source cached 1792065600, the 4 releases, one db_query (no write). Run 6 (origin 10): the registry sha256 of nightly-2026-10-18-1df370f is not the recorded one (a GitHub digest, given in compat.tsv): changed and dropped lines for it, the list has only the July release (its recorded sha256 is the same, so no write), the file of origin 10 is written (R-CV6: the two sources are checked together).
Run 7 (slice 204b, origin 11, Q340 and Q222): rows log 1 and 3 are one tag (nightly-2026-10-14) and target with 2 sha256, log 2 has size 0, log 4 and 5 are one tag and target with the same sha256. The first row of log 1 (the sha256 of run 1 for this tag and target, so no new pin) is the record, and the later row of log 3 is a change (R-CV6, R-IX4: the smaller log index is the record): changed and dropped lines for nightly-2026-10-14-38a3029, and the release is not in the list. The size 0 row is a release with no asset (an asset with no size is not an asset, R-AP80). The row of log 4 is a release with the size of its row, 7000 (not 7001 and not 0), and its pin is the one write (pinned=1). The file of origin 11 is written with the 5 rows. Also in runs 1 to 6: the size of an asset is the size of its row (1000 plus the log index), not 0 (R-CV3, R-AP80, Design Q340).
